{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "31", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "07", "M": "40", "S": "07"}}, "news": [{"title": "LIC Housing Finance\u2019s net profit rises 12% to \u20b91,506.59 crore in Q2 FY27", "para": "In Q2 FY27, LIC Housing Finance showcased a notable financial performance, with a net consolidated profit after tax of \u20b91,506.59 crore, reflecting an 11.7 percent increase. Their total disbursements climbed to \u20b918,127 crore, marking an 11 percent rise compared to last year. Additionally, the gross non-performing assets improved to 2.05 percent, down from 2.51 percent, and the first half's profit rose by 10.6 percent to \u20b93,005.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/housing-finance/lic-housing-finances-net-profit-rises-12-to-1506-59-crore-in-q2-fy27/135386308?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-1742310/135386308.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "housing-finance"}, {"title": "Delhi gears up for pollution curbs from November 1; construction ban among measures", "para": "Beginning November 1, Delhi is set to introduce crucial air pollution reduction measures. These initiatives will impose limitations on older vehicle models and prohibit construction activities that create dust. To further deter private car use, parking charges will rise, while both government and private offices will embrace staggered hours and remote work policies. Authorities will take action against open burning of waste and enforce penalties for offenders.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/delhi-gears-up-for-pollution-curbs-from-november-1-construction-ban-among-measures/135387913?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-260546/135387913.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Tamil Nadu sand truck owners announce three-day strike from November 1", "para": "From November 1 to 3, sand truck owners in Tamil Nadu are set to go on strike. This decision is rooted in their outcry against corruption within both transport and mining sectors. The Tamil Nadu State Sand Lorry Owners\u2019 Federation is advocating for a unified e-way bill system to deter illegal operations and insists on the installation of GPS tracking devices in mineral transport.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/allied-industries/tamil-nadu-sand-truck-owners-announce-three-day-strike-from-november-1/135387518?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-196452/135387518.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "allied-industries"}]}